  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: The top two configurations (config_029: 0.725, config_008: 0.721) both use imagenet_vit_l + transformer aggregation + multiprofile, with weighted fusion slightly edging out concat. However, all four completed experiments use scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder, leaving the RNA-encoder choice (scgpt, pca_n2000) completely unexplored. This is the largest remaining source of uncertainty. Question: Does scgpt, a larger generative-pretrained RNA model, outperform scvi_n200 when paired with the best-performing image/aggregation/fusion stack (imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted)? Why this experiment: config_010 isolates the RNA-encoder variable while holding every other component at its empirically best setting, giving a clean read on whether we should pivot to scgpt in subsequent experiments. It is the highest-information experiment available: if scgpt matches or beats 0.725, it opens a new exploitation direction; if it underperforms, we confirm scvi_n200 is optimal and can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning fusion/profile choices. Expected cost: scgpt is a larger pretrained model than scvi_n200, so I estimate ~5–7 GPU hours (moderately above config_029's 3.60 h), which is acceptable given the budget of 5 remaining experiments."
}

